    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0908" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg880"/>

                <head>487. Telegram From the Embassy in Canada to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d487-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-07-23T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1956—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Eyes only for the Secretary. Reference Deptels 33 and 34.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d487-f2"/> I talked to
                    Pearson afternoon July 23 and he is now reasonably optimistic over possibility
                    securing Prime Minister’s approval to prompt release of 12 F86s on basis of and
                    dependent on series of US actions contemplated in Deptel 33. He wants to talk to St. Laurent within 24 hours and
                    believes if he can convince him, there will be no difficulty with Cabinet later
                    this week. He would thereafter hope to announce in Parliament next week
                    immediate release 12 and tell Israel Government would consider later release
                    additional 12. He understands and accepts that US would not publicly announce
                    granting of arms export licenses but relies on US journalistic enterprise to
                    discover and publish. He now agrees multipartite ambassadorial consultation
                    would be unwise and after talking to Prime Minister, would be prepared to send
                    expert to Washington at any time in company of Ignatieff as cover. Latter is due
                    visit Washington shortly on NATO Wisemen
                    operation.</p>
                <p>For his talk with St. Laurent Pearson has asked me to provide him with top secret
                    personal note summarizing main points. I think it important I should do so and
                    next following telegram contains draft<anchor n="3" xml:id="d487-f3"/> which I
                    will deliver pending approval of text which I hope I can have telephonically
                    Tuesday morning. Pearson is fully cognizant <pb facs="0909" n="881"
                        xml:id="pg881"/> importance secrecy regarding Operation Stockpile though
                    thinks it will ultimately leak, including character its contents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Merchant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
